Title: The Widening Gyre
Order: 5
Production Code: 1x05

INT. VERGE COMPACT PICKET SHIP - BRIEFING ROOM - DAY

AMB: a cramped military interior, too many people for the room

[[Iyoha Sten]] has called the party aboard directly — no courier, no formality.

IYOHA STEN
I have three ships holding a perimeter meant for one, a Choir expedition that thinks the countdown's almost over, a Concern director who won't tell me what she's actually found, and now word that the Chain tried to rob you in open space. I would like, very much, for someone to tell me what is actually happening.

Let the party decide how much to share. Whatever they choose, Sten believes them — she's out of better options.

IYOHA STEN (CONT'D)
If that Key is what the Choir thinks it is, I need to know before it matters, not after.

MEV-KESH (V.O.)
(cutting in over an unsecured channel, uninvited)
It's already mattering, Commodore. You're just late to it.

Before Sten can respond, every console in the room alarms at once.

SFX: a klaxon, station-wide, not just this ship

Boxed text — read this slowly, it's the cliffhanger:

"Through the viewport, the Loom is changing. Not exploding, not collapsing — opening. A seam along the outer ring that wasn't there this morning splits wide, venting light nobody has an instrument name for. On every channel at once, every faction's ships start moving toward it at the same moment, and nobody asked anyone else first."

IYOHA STEN (CONT'D)
(already moving)
That's not a scouting opportunity. That's a starting gun.

MUSIC: STING - unresolved, cut hard

GM note: this is where the currently written material ends. Do not resolve what's behind the seam, whether the factions clash, or what happens to [[the Chord Key]] here — that's for whoever picks this campaign back up next. See world/notes/ for the live threads this leaves open.

GM note — contingencies: if the party never meets with Sten at all and this scene doesn't happen as written, the Loom's shift still occurs on schedule regardless — it isn't triggered by anything the party does. Simply describe it happening wherever they currently are, and let Sten (or whichever faction contact is nearest) react to it in person instead.
